Debugging Flow in Selenium
Test Execution
      ↓
Test Fails
      ↓
Read Error Message
      ↓
Identify Failure Point
      ↓
Analyze Root Cause
      ↓
Fix Script/Application
      ↓
Re-run Test
      ↓
Verify Result

Common Selenium Errors
A. NoSuchElementException--->driver.find_element(By.ID, "username123")|
                                                                    |
 solution -> WebDriverWait(driver,10).until(
    EC.presence_of_element_located((By.ID,"username"))
) 

B.  TimeoutException
problem -
 WebDriverWait(driver,5).until(
    EC.visibility_of_element_located((By.ID,"login"))
)
solution - WebDriverWait(driver,15)

c. StaleElementRefrenceException 
problem - page refreshed after element locating 
button.click()
driver.refresh()

button.click()
-------------------------------------------------------------
BreakPoint -A breakpoint pauses execution at a specific line.
example -
       driver.get("hhtps://google.com")
       search_box = driver.find_element(BY.NAME , "q") <-breakpoint
       send_keys("python")
   

Debugging Tech -
1) Print statement --  print("step 1") 
                  driver.get("https://google.com")
                       print("setp 2)
                  x = driver.find_element(By.NAME , "x")
                       print("step 3)
                       send_keys("hello")
2) Logging --- 
         import Logging
         Logging.baseConfig(level= logging.info)
         logging.info("LoggingInfo")

3) ScreentShot 
         driver.save_screenshot("debug.png")

4) Browser Inspection
         crtl+ shift + i 
         F12
         right click menu->inspect                   
5) Explicit Wait
         WebDriverWait(driver,10).until(
    EC.visibility_of_element_located((By.ID,"login"))
    )

Q1. What is debugging?

Finding and fixing issues in automation scripts.

Q2. What tools do you use for debugging?
Breakpoints
Print statements
Logging
Screenshots
Browser DevTools
Q3. What is a breakpoint?
A marker that pauses execution and allows inspection of variables and application state.

Q4. How do you debug dynamic elements?
Explicit waits
Verify locator
Check iframe
Check DOM updates
Re-locate element
Q5. How do you debug failed Selenium tests?
Read exception.
Check locator.
Add logs.
Take screenshot.
Verify waits.
Reproduce manually.

==========================================================
Screenshot Tech- 

1) Full Page /Browser screenshot 
            driver.save_screenshot("error.png")

2)Specific Element Screenshot
            element.screenshot("error123.png")

Q3. Why are screenshots important?

They help in debugging, reporting, and providing evidence of test execution.

Q4. When should screenshots be captured?
On test failure
After successful transactions
During UI validation
Before/after critical actions
Q5. Which screenshot method is most commonly used in automation frameworks?
driver.save_screenshot()

because it captures the complete browser state and is typically attached to reports when tests fail.

===========================================================
Reporting 
-----------
Reporting is the process of generating a document or 
dashboard that shows the result of test execution.
Advantages of Reporting
1. Easy Analysis

Know which tests passed and failed.

2. Failure Investigation

Reports show:

Error messages
Stack traces
Screenshots
3. Evidence

Proof that testing was executed.

4. Better Communication

Developers and managers can quickly review results.

5. Historical Tracking

Compare results across multiple executions.
---------------
Types of Reports in Selenium-
1) simple text report 
 example - report = open("report.txt", "w")

report.write("Login Test - PASS")

report.close()

2) HTML Report

   <table>
<tr>
<td>Login Test</td>
<td>PASS</td>
</tr>
</table>

3) Extent Report - Most popular in automation projects.
   Features:

Pie charts
Screenshots
Categories
Dashboard

4) Allure Report--Common in PyTest frameworks.

When is Reporting Required?
Case 1: Daily Regression Execution
Case 2: Release Testing

Before production deployment:
Case 3: Client Demo

Need evidence:
Case 4: CI/CD Pipeline

Example:
Jenkins
Azure DevOps
GitHub Actions

Case 5: Failure Analysis

==========================================
Q1. What is reporting in Selenium?

Reporting is the process of generating execution results showing pass/fail status, execution details, screenshots, and errors.

Q2. Why do we use reports?

To analyze results, track failures, provide evidence, and communicate test outcomes.

Q3. What information should a report contain?
Test Name
Status
Execution Time
Error Message
Screenshot
Environment Details
Q4. Which reporting tools have you used?
PyTest HTML Reports
Allure Reports
Extent Reports
Q5. Why attach screenshots to reports?

Screenshots provide visual evidence and help developers quickly identify failures.

=============================================================================
How do you maintain screenshots in large automation projects?

Answer:

Store in dedicated Screenshot folder
Use timestamps
Organize by execution date
Delete old screenshots periodically
from datetime import datetime

timestamp = datetime.now().strftime("%Y%m%d_%H%M%S")
driver.save_screenshot(f"Login_{timestamp}.png")
-------------------------------------------------------------------

What challenges have you faced with screenshots?

Answer:

Dynamic pages loading slowly
Capturing before page fully loads
Overwriting old screenshots
Large storage consumption
--------------------------------------------------
Q- How do you attach screenshots to reports?
import allure

allure.attach.file(
    "failure.png",
    name="Failure Screenshot",
    attachment_type=allure.attachment_type.PNG
)
----------------------------------------------------
Explain a real-time debugging issue you resolved.

Answer:

During login automation, scripts were intermittently failing with
 NoSuchElementException. Investigation showed the page was loading slowly. 
I replaced static waits with Explicit Waits and the issue was resolved.
------------------------------------------------------------
| Debugging            | Logging                  |
| -------------------- | ------------------------ |
| Manual investigation | Automated record keeping |
| Uses breakpoints     | Uses log statements      |
| Real-time analysis   | Historical analysis      |
----------------------------------------------------------

Screenshot is not getting captured. How will you investigate?

Answer:

Verify file path
Check write permissions
Ensure browser session is active
Check exception logs
-------------------------------------------------------
Report shows FAIL but screenshot is missing. What could be the reason?

Answer:

Screenshot code not executed
Wrong screenshot path
Driver already closed
File permission issue

Q-How do you debug StaleElementReferenceException?
Relocate element 
button = driver.find_element(By.ID, "submit")
button.click()

Q-Which is more important in a framework: Reporting or Screenshots?

Answer:
Both are important. Reporting provides execution summary, while screenshots provide
 visual proof of failures. Together they make troubleshooting much faster.
 